From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32: the folder view's icon sizes, thumbnails, tiles and groups

IFolderView2::SetViewModeAndIconSize/GetViewModeAndIconSize: Medium (48),
Large (96) and Extra large (256) icons in an image list of the view's own,
each icon taken from the best system list and a file's thumbnail made on a
thread of the view's (newest request first) and put in when it comes. Tiles
(FVM_TILE: 250 px, the type and size under the name) and Content (FVM_CONTENT:
a row across the view, the type under the name, "Date modified" and "Size" on
the right) on the list view's tile view. IFolderView2::SetGroupBy/GetGroupBy
by Name (0 - 9, A - H, I - P, Q - Z, Other), Date modified (Today, Yesterday,
Earlier this week, ... A long time ago), Type and Size (Empty, Tiny, ...
Gigantic), each header with its count, kept as files come and go. Icons fill
rows, as in File Explorer (the desktop's still fill columns). A selected
icon's whole box is tinted. A file opened from the view is added to the recent
documents (Quick access); SHAddToRecentDocs makes a Unicode shortcut for a
name the ANSI code page cannot spell (the rest of it is still ANSI). The
keyboard's context menu opens at the focused item.

